# Vedic Neev — production environment template.
#
# Copy every key below into your Vercel project's Environment Variables
# (Production scope; add to Preview too if preview deploys should hit the
# same Supabase project — otherwise give Preview its own). See
# `.env.example` for the local-dev version of this file (same variables,
# same required-vs-optional split).
#
# Required vs optional at a glance:
#   REQUIRED — DATABASE_URL, DIRECT_URL, NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL
#   OPTIONAL — RAZORPAY_*, WHATSAPP_*, NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_*,
#              SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY (each runs a clearly `mock: true`
#              fallback in code when unset — the app deploys and works in
#              demo mode even before you have real credentials; see the
#              Auth section below for what "real" means for sign-in)

# ── Database — REQUIRED (packages/db, apps/web/app/api) ──────────────────
# packages/db's schema targets Supabase Postgres. apps/web calls it
# directly on two flows: apps/web/app/api/auth/sync/route.ts (every OTP
# sign-in) and apps/web/app/api/exam/submit/route.ts (every mock-test
# submit) — both throw/500 without a reachable database. These variables
# are also what `npm run db:push` / `npm run db:seed` use to provision the
# schema and reference data (exam templates, question bank, media catalog).
# Everything else in the app (test-taking, results, Mistake Vault, Parent
# Command Center) runs client-side in Zustand + localStorage regardless.

# Pooled connection (via Supabase's pgbouncer, port 6543) — used at runtime.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:your-password@db.your-project.supabase.co:6543/postgres?pgbouncer=true

# Direct connection (port 5432, no pgbouncer) — required for `prisma db push`
# and `prisma migrate deploy`, which need a session-mode connection.
DIRECT_URL=postgresql://postgres:your-password@db.your-project.supabase.co:5432/postgres

# ── Auth — OPTIONAL, mock fallback ────────────────────────────────────────
# All three unset → phone/OTP sign-in stays a fully client-side mock
# (apps/web/src/lib/auth/mockAuthProvider.ts — OTP always "123456", nothing
# issued/verified server-side, no real user session anywhere). All three
# set → the apps/web/app/api/auth/whatsapp/send-otp and verify-otp routes
# (backed by apps/web/src/lib/auth/whatsappOtpServer.ts) generate and hash a
# real 6-digit code (packages/db's PhoneOtp table), delivers it over
# WhatsApp using the WHATSAPP_* credentials below (NOT Supabase's own phone
# provider, which requires a separate paid SMS gateway this project isn't
# using), then uses the service-role Admin API to bridge a verified code
# into a real Supabase session. Once set, apps/web/app/api/razorpay/verify-payment/route.ts
# and the OTP route itself stop trusting any client-supplied phone/id and
# require that real session instead (401 without one) — see
# apps/web/src/lib/supabase/env.ts's isSupabaseAuthConfigured.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key
# Secret — server-only, never exposed to the client. Supabase dashboard →
# Project Settings → API → service_role key. Only apps/web/src/lib/supabase/admin.ts
# uses it, to create/confirm the Supabase auth user and mint their session
# after a WhatsApp OTP verifies — treat it with the same care as a database
# superuser password; it bypasses every RLS policy.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
#
# ── Ecosystem note: sharing identity with Vedic Mind AI (vedicmindai.in) ──
# Recognizing the same person on both vedicneev.com and vedicmindai.in
# requires that product's own deployment to point NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL /
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY / SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY at this SAME
# Supabase project (not a project of its own) — that's what makes a
# Supabase-authenticated user a shared identity instead of two unrelated
# accounts. That's a change to Vedic Mind AI's own infrastructure/codebase,
# outside this repo, and isn't done by anything here. Once both apps share
# a project, User.vedicMindAiUserId (packages/db/prisma/schema.prisma) is
# reserved for whatever cross-app account-linking key that integration
# ends up needing.

# ── Institute Suite (omrtest.vedicneev.com) — OPTIONAL until that app is deployed ──
# Set on BOTH the apps/web and apps/omrtest Vercel projects, to the same
# value, once omrtest.vedicneev.com is live — this is what makes the
# Supabase session cookie set by either app's login readable by the other.
# Must be a leading-dot parent domain (".vedicneev.com"); see
# apps/web/src/lib/supabase/env.ts's getSupabaseCookieOptions.
NEXT_PUBLIC_COOKIE_DOMAIN=.vedicneev.com
# Where apps/web's header/footer "For Institutes" links point — see
# apps/web/src/lib/institute/instituteUrl.ts.
NEXT_PUBLIC_INSTITUTE_APP_URL=https://omrtest.vedicneev.com
# Set on the apps/typingtest Vercel project once typingtest.vedicneev.com
# is live — must share NEXT_PUBLIC_COOKIE_DOMAIN above and the same
# Supabase project as apps/web for the shared-domain session to work.
NEXT_PUBLIC_TYPINGTEST_APP_URL=https://typingtest.vedicneev.com

# ── Admin panel (apps/web/src/lib/admin/session.ts) — REQUIRED to use /admin ──
# Shared-secret password gating /admin (the blog draft queue) — a real,
# functional gate (HMAC-signed session cookie via middleware.ts), but a
# single shared password, not a per-user account system. Use a long random
# value in production. Leave unset to disable /admin entirely.
ADMIN_ACCESS_KEY=

# ── Razorpay (apps/web/src/lib/payments/razorpayServer.ts) — OPTIONAL ────
# All three unset → mock checkout (a "Simulate Successful Payment" demo
# flow, no real gateway or charge). Key pair set → real order creation +
# HMAC-SHA256 signature verification against Razorpay's live API. Use LIVE
# (not test) keys from the Razorpay dashboard for a real production
# deployment. RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET is separate — from the webhook
# endpoint you register at https://vedicneev.com/api/webhook/payment in the
# Razorpay dashboard — and is required for the storefront's one-time
# product purchases to fulfill automatically on payment.captured.
RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=
RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# ── WhatsApp Cloud API — OPTIONAL, shared by two features ────────────────
# apps/web/app/api/whatsapp/send-report/route.ts (diagnostic reports) and,
# once the Auth vars above are also set, the WhatsApp OTP login routes under
# apps/web/app/api/auth/whatsapp/
# (login codes). Both unset → both features run mock (payload/code logged
# server-side, nothing sent). Both set → real POSTs to
# https://graph.facebook.com/{version}/{WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID}/messages.
WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID=
WHATSAPP_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# Optional — all three have working defaults ("v20.0", "auth_login", "en").
# WHATSAPP_API_VERSION parameterizes the OTP route's URL and
# apps/web/src/lib/whatsapp/whatsappService.ts's Graph API calls —
# send-report hardcodes its own "v20.0" constant and does not read this
# var. WHATSAPP_TEMPLATE_NAME/WHATSAPP_TEMPLATE_LANG must name a template
# (and one of its approved languages) already live in Meta's Authentication
# category with one body parameter (the code) — approve it in Meta
# Business Manager first; this project has no way to create/approve it
# from code. A name or language that doesn't match an approved template
# exactly produces Meta error #132001 ("Template name does not exist in
# the translation").
WHATSAPP_API_VERSION=
WHATSAPP_TEMPLATE_NAME=
WHATSAPP_TEMPLATE_LANG=
# Optional, defaults to "NONE" (body-only, no button component sent) — set
# this only if the approved template above was actually created with a
# button. Meta's WhatsApp Manager defaults new Authentication templates to
# including a one-tap button, and sending a body-only payload against a
# template that has one is a common cause of error #131008 ("Required
# parameter is missing"). "COPY_CODE" for a "Copy Code" button, "URL" for a
# one-tap autofill/link button — check WhatsApp Manager → Message Templates
# → your template to see which (if either) it has.
WHATSAPP_TEMPLATE_BUTTON_TYPE=
# Required only for apps/web/app/api/whatsapp/webhook/route.ts (inbound
# messages + delivery statuses from Meta). Set to any secret string, then
# enter that same value as the "Verify token" when configuring the webhook
# URL in Meta App Dashboard → WhatsApp → Configuration — Meta echoes it
# back on the one-time GET handshake to prove you own the endpoint. Leave
# unset to have the webhook's GET handler always reject verification (503).
WHATSAPP_WEBHOOK_VERIFY_TOKEN=

# ── Vercel Cron ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Required for app/api/cron/seed-sprints/route.ts (schedules next Sunday's
# National Sprints weekly — see apps/web/vercel.json's "crons" entry). Any
# secret string; Vercel automatically sends it back as
# `Authorization: Bearer <value>` when it invokes a Cron project's own
# routes, once this same value is set in that project's environment
# variables. Leave unset to have the route always reject with 500.
CRON_SECRET=

# ── App origin — REQUIRED for correct metadata ───────────────────────────
# Absolute base URL of this deployment. Used for metadataBase — canonical
# URLs, OG/Twitter image resolution, robots.txt, and sitemap.xml — in
# apps/web/src/lib/siteConfig.ts. Must be the exact origin that actually
# serves production traffic (bare vs `www.`, and whichever of the custom
# domain or the vercel.app default is canonical) or every generated
# canonical/OG/sitemap URL will point at the wrong place.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://vedicneev.com
